{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And I will walk in your midst.</b> The meaning of 'walking' is going to and fro, not to one place alone. He said: if so, 'I will walk in your midst' — for the efflux of the Glory will not descend to one place alone, as it was in the Tabernacle and the Temple, as it says: וְעָשւוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְתִּי בְּתוֹכָם (Exodus 25:8) — that is, in this manner and in that place alone I will dwell among them. He explained this in saying אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לְךָ שָׁמָּה (Exodus 30:6), וְנוֹעַדְתִּי שָׁמָּה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 29:43). But 'I will walk in your midst' — and My Glory will be seen in every place where you are, for in truth wherever the righteous of the generation are, He is the holy habitation of the Most High, in whom His intention is fulfilled, as it says: הַשָּׁמַיִם כִּסְאִי וְהָאָרֶץ הֲדֹם רַגְלָי, וְאֶל זֶה אַבִּיט, אֶל עָנִי וּנְכֵה רוּחַ וְחָרֵד עַל דְּבָרִי (Isaiah 66:1–2)." "<b>And I will be your Elohim.</b> I will be an Elohim uniquely devoted to you — you will have no Elohim or guide besides Me. And so the eternity of your existence will be from Me without intermediary, as it is for the other separate, eternal beings, when you are then in My image, after My likeness — as was the intention in the creation of man and in the giving of Torah. Therefore He said: וְלָקַחְתִּי אֶתְכֶם לִי לְעָם וְהָיִיתִי לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים (Exodus 6:7), for in truth at the giving of Torah, had they not corrupted, the intention was to establish them at the perfection of the days of the Messiah and the world to come, which He promises in this chapter without doubt. Indeed in the passage אַתֶּם נִצָּבִים (Deuteronomy 29:12) He said that the intention is that He establish them as a people so that He would be their Elohim, but He did not promise that it would be so then. But the continual service of the Tabernacle, in His saying וְשָׁכַנְתִּי בְּתוֹךְ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְהָיִיתִי לָהֶם לֵאלֹהִים (Exodus 29:45), He promised in every respect as this chapter. But in the other places He said לִהְיוֹת לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי לְעָם — that the whole aim of your faces should be to do My will and to serve Me with one accord without doubt, as is fitting for every nation to do for its true king."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The last quotation, לִהְיוֹת לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי לְעָם, recurs in several passages (e.g. Leviticus 11:45, 22:32–33, 25:38, etc.); Sforno does not specify which he means by 'the other places.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:21.336584389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}